  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Korea deposited the letter of ratifying ILO Conventions C.29, C.87 and C.98 in April 2021. It is as a consequence of the joint advocacy and campaign by the Federation of Korean Trade Unions (FKTU) and the Korea Confederation of Trade Unions (KCTU), after overcoming fragmented relationship between the FKTU and the KCTU.  

In regards to the COVID-19 response, the FKTU submitted a series of recommendations to the Economic, Social and Labour Council (ESLC), demanding emergency measures for job security and wage protection. The ESLC is a tripartite body where the FKTU joins. This resulted in the establishment of a special committee dealing with social, employment and re-structuring aspects of the crisis. The FKTU in its follow-up submission highlights the need for the prohibition of dismissals. They call on to extend the access to employment retention schemes to further categories of workers including public bus drivers, who see their working time decreasing, and carriers, aircraft ground handling companies, and subcontractors. 
The FKTU&apos;s initiative was joined by the KCTU and for the first time in 21 years, the FKTU and the KCTU jointly engaged in tripartite dialogues in May resulting to reach an agreement on &#x2018;The Tripartite Declaration on Overcoming COVID-19&apos; in July. The parties agreed to make joint efforts to retain employees instead of laying them off by making full use of working hour reduction and leave of absence schemes. The plan under the declaration also included for an employment safety net to bolster job security, reflecting the joint demand by the unions, which was a comprehensive employment guarantee and dismissal prohibitions as well as the expansion of the mandatory employment insurance to more worker categories. The ILO provided the FKTU and the KCTU with finance and technical inputs in organising joint forums and conducting a research work analysing the labour law in line with C.87 and C.98.

The ILO provided technical support to raise awareness of FKTU and KCTU on further legislative amendment and effective implementation of the conventions.</narrative>
   </description>
